-- title:
--   Fourier identification from almost-everywhere Cesaro convergence
-- statement:
--   Assume that the Cesaro approximants to the complexified interpolation derivative $G_C$ converge to it almost everywhere. Then the Fourier transform of $G_C$ is the continuous, compactly supported Vaaler transform $\widehat J$.
